# List Performance (Telegram-level)

## Chat message list (ChatScreen) — LazyColumn

```kotlin
LazyColumn(
    modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),
    state = listState,
    reverseLayout = true
) {
    items(
        count = messages.size,
        key = { messages[messages.size - 1 - it].id },
        contentType = { if (messages[messages.size - 1 - it].isMe) 0 else 1 }
    ) { index ->
        MessageBubble(messages[messages.size - 1 - index])
    }
}
```

### Rules
- Always provide `key` (Long) for efficient diffing
- Always provide `contentType` to enable item reuse across types
- Use index-based `items(count)` with reverse indexing — zero allocation (no `asReversed()`)
- Use `reverseLayout = true` for chat — newest at bottom
- `derivedStateOf` for load-more trigger and jump-to-bottom visibility
- Auto-scroll on new messages only when user is already at bottom

## MessageBubble rules

- `remember(msg.content)` for `parseContentText()` — avoid re-parsing on recomposition
- `remember(msg.timestampSeconds)` for `formatRelativeTime()` — avoid re-computing
- Pre-compute shapes as top-level vals: `BubbleShapeSent`, `BubbleShapeReceived`
- All colors from `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` — dark mode works automatically

```kotlin
@Composable
fun MessageBubble(msg: MessageEntity) {
    val content = remember(msg.content) { parseContentText(msg.content) }
    val time = remember(msg.timestampSeconds) { formatRelativeTime(msg.timestampSeconds) }
    // ...
}
```

## DM list (MessagesScreen) — LazyColumn

For shorter lists (< 200 items), `LazyColumn` is ideal:

```kotlin
LazyColumn(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
    items(
        items = state.messages,
        key = { it.channelId },
        contentType = { it.type }
    ) { dm ->
        val timeText = remember(dm.lastMessageTimestamp) { formatRelativeTime(dm.lastMessageTimestamp) }
        DmListItem(dm = dm, timeText = timeText, onClick = { ... })
    }
}
```

## Scroll performance rules

- Auto-scroll to bottom only when user is within 1-2 items of the latest message
- `loadMoreTop` trigger: when `lastVisiblePosition >= totalItems - 3`
- Guard against duplicate loads: check `isLoadingMore` flag
- FloatingActionButton for jump-to-bottom when `firstVisibleItemIndex > 5`

## Shared parsing utility

All content parsing and time formatting uses `util/ContentParser.kt`:
- `parseContentText(content)` — full text with newlines
- `parseContentPreview(content)` — single-line preview for DM list
- `formatRelativeTime(epochSeconds)` — "now", "5m", "2h", "14:30"
- Regex compiled once as `private val` at file level
